post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'

==> simpleEMS runs on its own Python 3.13 in /opt/simpleems (system Python
    is 3.14, which has no cadquery-ocp wheels). Your system Python is untouched.
    Use the CLI:                        simpleems
    Run library code with its venv:     /opt/simpleems/venv/bin/python

==> The FDTD solver stack (CSXCAD + openEMS Python bindings) is NOT included:
    simpleEMS.components and 13 other modules import CSXCAD/openEMS at module
    level and will fail with ModuleNotFoundError. The AUR `openems` package
    cannot help -- its bindings are built for the system Python 3.14, not 3.13.

    Build the stack against the bundled interpreter (10-30 min):
      sudo /opt/simpleems/venv/bin/simpleems install openems --prefix /opt/openEMS
      sudo ln -s /opt/openEMS/bin/openEMS /usr/local/bin/

EOF
}
post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}
